  ⭐⭐⭐ THE CONSTRUCTION A THIRD PARTY ACTUALLY PERFORMS, END TO END. Bring their layer in.
  Make my layer beside it. Make a THIRD layer out of BOTH. And separate all three afterwards.

    as-filed        one part, FOREIGN   the bakery's oven line, carried through unchanged
    as-contracted   no part, ORIGINATED the same line, read a second way
    both-views      two parts, LOCAL    made out of the two above

  ⛔⛔ THE THIRD FUSION IS THE ONE THAT COULD NOT BE WRITTEN BEFORE, and only one thing had to
  change to allow it: a filing can now say WHICH FILING IT IS. A part whose notation matches
  this document's own is a local part. There is no second kind of part and no new element on
  `asrt:Part` — the distinction is a string comparison against the filing's own name.

  ⭐⭐⭐ AND THE ALTERNATION IS AN ORDINARY FUSION WITH AN ELIMINATION, NOT A NEW RELATION.
  Two views of ONE quantity summed is that quantity COUNTED TWICE, which is exactly what
  `Elimination` removes. `EliminationAgainst/demand` is literally "what was ASKED, counted
  twice".

    Σ parts demand      [3600, 4000, 4800]       Σ parts nameplate  [4320, 4320, 4320]
    eliminate           [1800, 2000, 2400]       eliminate          [2160, 2160, 2160]
    composed            [1800, 2000, 2400] ✓     composed           [2160, 2160, 2160] ✓

  ⛔ THE ELIMINATED COPY IS THE WHOLE INTERVAL, NOT A POINT, and getting that wrong is the
  first mistake this fixture caught — in the hand that wrote it. `Elimination` subtracts
  COMPONENT-WISE and does not reverse bounds, because it removes "a COMPONENT OF THE VERY
  FIGURE IT IS REMOVED FROM". For two views of one quantity that argument is not merely
  applicable, it is exact: the removed copy IS the figure, so it moves with it at every bound.

  ⚠️ AND THE SUM RULE STAYS EXACT THROUGH IT. A checker owes the same arithmetic here as for
  any other fusion; nothing is suspended and nothing is special-cased. That is the test of
  whether the composition answer was the right one — if it needed the rule relaxed, it was not.

  ⭐ WHY THE TWO VIEWS ARE NOT THE SAME DOCUMENT. Identical magnitudes throughout, and the
  HOLDERS differ: `as-filed` puts the shortfall on `people`, which no instrument reaches;
  `as-contracted` puts it on `counterparty`, which invoices. Same number, one invisible and one
  recoverable. Nobody is wrong and nothing was corrected — the second reading is what makes the
  quantity legible, which is this model's own thesis pointed at a filing instead of a business.
-->
